{"uid":"1a16d6fb079a4e79","name":"test_the_installed_layout_grants_a_non_owner_read_and_exec_but_never_write","fullName":"tests.test_commit_scan_engine_boundary#test_the_installed_layout_grants_a_non_owner_read_and_exec_but_never_write","historyId":"7b95510e050a882d1836f16e28fb8500","time":{"start":1791935079297,"stop":1791935079328,"duration":31},"description":"Task cure-01-02, requirement I.1/DoD 9: the boundary this task ships\n    is *not* \"no write bit anywhere\" -- the hook has to stay readable and\n    executable by the agent uid, because git spawns the hook processes from\n    the worker's own `git commit`/`git push` at that uid. What protects it\n    is the OTHER-class permission of the root-owned layout: `r-x` on the\n    directory and the hook (traverse, list, read, exec) and no `w` on\n    either -- and since a directory-entry operation (`unlink`, `rename`,\n    `replace`, create) is gated by the PARENT directory's write bit, an\n    agent-uid process has no way to reach any entry in it.\n\n    This states the permission CLASSES the installer actually produces,\n    rather than only checking `mode & 0o022 == 0` the way the pre-R2 node\n    above does; the syscall-level denial at a real second uid is\n    `tests/test_commit_scan_hooks_docker.py`'s job.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-02, requirement I.1/DoD 9: the boundary this task ships<br />\nis <em>not</em> &quot;no write bit anywhere&quot; -- the hook has to stay readable and<br />\nexecutable by the agent uid, because git spawns the hook processes from<br />\nthe worker's own <code>git commit</code>/<code>git push</code> at that uid. What protects it<br />\nis the OTHER-class permission of the root-owned layout: <code>r-x</code> on the<br />\ndirectory and the hook (traverse, list, read, exec) and no <code>w</code> on<br />\neither -- and since a directory-entry operation (<code>unlink</code>, <code>rename</code>,<br />\n<code>replace</code>, create) is gated by the PARENT directory's write bit, an<br />\nagent-uid process has no way to reach any entry in it.</p>\n<pre><code>This states the permission CLASSES the installer actually produces,\nrather than only checking `mode &amp; 0o022 == 0` the way the pre-R2 node\nabove does; the syscall-level denial at a real second uid is\n`tests/test_commit_scan_hooks_docker.py`'s job.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791934845932,"stop":1791934845932,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791934845932,"stop":1791934845933,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791935079275,"stop":1791935079275,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791935079275,"stop":1791935079283,"duration":8},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791935079284,"stop":1791935079284,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791935079284,"stop":1791935079289,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"paramet